    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30451" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nătātĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that can swim</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Herm. 33</span></i>
			. —<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nătātĭles</span></b> ,
				ĭum, m., <i>swimming creatures</i>: feras, volucres, reptiles, natatiles,
			Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 10, 332;
					<i><span class="en">App. de Mund. 28</span></i>.</div>
